    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-18620" textLabel="ent-cassadiene-C2-hydroxylase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q6YV88" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="O-28, hartmut">The cDNA for a diterpene olefin 2&amp;alpha;-hydroxylase from &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt; has been codon optimized, N-terminally modified and expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. The cytochrome P450 dependent monooxygenase (CYP71Z7) hydroxylated |FRAME:CPD-4751 &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-cassa-12,15-diene| at C-2&amp;alpha; forming the respective |FRAME:CPD-16719 2&amp;alpha;-hydroxy-&lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-cassadiene|. However, the reaction efficiency is rather low and CYP71Z7 is thought to be involved in an later step of the phytocassanes biosynthesis, i.e. the C2-hydroxylation of |FRAME:CPD-16675 3&amp;beta;-hydroxy-12,15-cassadiene-11-one| yielding |FRAME:CPD-16676 2&amp;beta;,3&amp;beta;-dihydroxy-12,15-cassadiene-11-one| |CITS:[21985968]| which has been proposed earlier |CITS:[16956633]|. CYP71Z7 is discussed as a gene which has been duplicated from CYP71Z6 and underwent a neofunctionalization in the chromosome 2 biosynthetic cluster |CITS:[21985968]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-18620" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phytozome" value="Os02t0570700-01" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q6YV88" />
